From 5eaacc698085b94740b120905dd289957f46031b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:41:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webdriverio): return multi-remote results from custom$,
 react$ and shadow$

On a multi-remote browser only `$` and `$$` were turned into a
`MultiRemoteElement` / `MultiRemoteElementArray`. `custom$`, `react$`,
`shadow$` and their `$$` variants returned one raw result per instance,
so they had no `isMultiRemote`, `getInstance()` or `select()`, element
commands could not run on them, and the list metadata (`selector`,
`foundWith`, `parent`, `props`) was missing.

Send these queries down the same paths as `$` and `$$`. The `$$`
variants keep their own `foundWith` and `props`, like the single-session
lists. Update the multi-remote types, the typings test and the docs that
described the old behavior.

Closes #15851
